English (United States) as the phone's default language and region (OH's own default is Chinese: i18n.para sets
const.global.language=zh-Hans, locale zh-Hans-CN, region CN). The product parameter file is in the chipset layer,
which init reads before /system/etc/param; the first value given to a const parameter stands (the same way the
port's const.distributed_file_property.enabled=false overrides the system's true). A language chosen in Settings
(persist.global.*) still wins over this default.

diff --git a/fajita/etc/para/product_fajita.para b/fajita/etc/para/product_fajita.para
index b28a988..a72a21f 100644
--- a/fajita/etc/para/product_fajita.para
+++ b/fajita/etc/para/product_fajita.para
@@ -38,3 +38,9 @@ const.SystemCapability.Applications.settings.Core=true
 # fails StartUser, user 100 is never unlocked, and SceneBoard starts no app that is not a system app
 # (ERR_BLOCK_START_FIRST_BOOT_SCREEN_UNLOCK).
 const.distributed_file_property.enabled=false
+
+# OnePlus 6 port: English (United States) by default. OH's i18n.para defaults to Chinese (zh-Hans, CN); this file
+# (chipset layer) is read before /system/etc/param, and the first value given to a const parameter stands.
+const.global.language=en-Latn-US
+const.global.locale=en-Latn-US
+const.global.region=US
